1
00:00:01,755 --> 00:00:05,290
Literate is a free, open-source way to
listen to articles,

2
00:00:05,885 --> 00:00:08,430
selected text, and local PDFs.

3
00:00:08,765 --> 00:00:13,070
There are two voice options. Instant uses
installed device voices.

4
00:00:13,625 --> 00:00:16,445
Natural uses Kokoro, with an initial model
download.

5
00:00:16,445 --> 00:00:19,190
The files stay cached for later reading.

6
00:00:19,505 --> 00:00:24,010
On an article, you can listen to the main
text with words highlighted as it plays.

7
00:00:24,665 --> 00:00:29,150
Selected passages also have a right-click
option: Read selection aloud.

8
00:00:29,925 --> 00:00:33,270
The section picker lets you focus on a
particular part of the page,

9
00:00:33,605 --> 00:00:36,850
leaving sidebars and related stories
outside the reading area.

10
00:00:37,325 --> 00:00:41,365
The mini-player keeps scrolling text
nearby. You can click individual words

11
00:00:41,365 --> 00:00:45,305
to jump around, or pin the player above
other windows in supported browsers.

12
00:00:45,305 --> 00:00:50,470
Speed, light and dark modes, and accent
colors can all be adjusted.

13
00:00:51,105 --> 00:00:53,010
Periwinkle is the starting color.

14
00:00:53,605 --> 00:00:58,065
Local PDFs are supported with Chrome’s
file-access permission. The reader

15
00:00:58,065 --> 00:01:02,810
works with existing text, while scanned
documents need text recognition first.

16
00:01:03,245 --> 00:01:08,310
The speech runs on your device. Kokoro’s
files download from Hugging Face,

17
00:01:08,405 --> 00:01:12,350
and the source page needs to remain open
while the mini-player is in use.
